  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Completeness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The agent made a deliberate trigger decision for all five workflows: path filters on deploy and docs-site, nothing changed for the schedule-only and issue-driven ones, and the required unit-tests check got the correct shape (a single workflow, no workflow-level paths or paths-ignore, a computed `salient` output gating setup-node, npm ci and npm test with `if:`, no companion skip workflow); one small flaw is that the PR diff compares base.sha to head.sha directly rather than from their merge-base, so a stale base can make it run when nothing salient changed."
      },
      {
        "name": "Salience",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "Each list matches what that workflow's steps actually use (src/test/package*.json for npm ci and npm test, scripts/deploy.sh plus sources for deploy, docs/ and mkdocs.yml for the docs site, each including its own workflow file), with no catch-alls or copies between workflows, though the agent did not check whether the tests read other config files such as a test-runner or tsconfig file."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The agent left nightly-sweep.yml, triage.yml and the branch-protection ruleset untouched, created no extra files, and only reported the unpinned mkdocs and the missing workflow_dispatch rather than changing them."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 8.9
